{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1447745-how-hard-would-it-be-to-convert-1e-content-to-2e","id":1447745,"title":"How hard would it be to convert 1e content to 2e?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-06T18:40:20-07:00","id":1447745,"title":"How hard would it be to convert 1e content to 2e?","content":"Title says it all. I don't know Chronicles well enough to know honestly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T18:51:09-07:00","id":1447748,"title":"","content":"Depends heavily on gameline and specific material. Some stuff is built on things that aren't true anymore or mechanical structures that have changed dramatically. Anything outside of Vampire that references a sin/breaking point equivalent at a specific rating in Integrity-analog is going to need to adjust to the new system's risk mechanism, for example. Did you have anything in mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T18:56:01-07:00","id":1447750,"title":"","content":"Like, me and several people here have been converting Legacies in Mage for a while, so <i>some</i> things are relatively easier. (Same holds for Bloodlines in Vampire)<br /> <br /> Both Bloodlines and Legacies are things where the writers gave out broad structural guidelines on how they\u2019re supposed to be built, which is why they\u2019re easier. It might be trickier without such guidelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T19:15:54-07:00","id":1447753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1447745-how-hard-would-it-be-to-convert-1e-content-to-2e?p=1447748#post1447748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends heavily on gameline and specific material. Some stuff is built on things that aren't true anymore or mechanical structures that have changed dramatically. Anything outside of Vampire that references a sin/breaking point equivalent at a specific rating in Integrity-analog is going to need to adjust to the new system's risk mechanism, for example. Did you have anything in mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wondering mostly. Bloodlines / Disciplines for VTR namely. Ultimately the main thing discouraging me is the fact 1e has a lot of material that never made it to 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T20:38:33-07:00","id":1447759,"title":"","content":"Super easy except when it's not.<br /> <br /> A lot of bloodlines and disciplines can just convert straight over without needing to alter anything more than, say, reducing +N weapon bonuses to (N-1) weapon ratings. Others need fundamental rewriting of their mechanics. It's all about whether they hook into the major system changes for Second Edition's base system and the Second Edition vampire template: the removal of derangements and of the Predator's Taint, the new vampiric Anchors, the altered clan banes, Discipline changes like the removal of aggravated damage from the core Protean progression. Abjurism: easy-peasy, insert as is with no changes at all (but the base Septemi bloodline weakness references Virtues which vampires no longer have). Despond: the top levels need to be wholly rewritten, because one inflicts derangements, which no longer exist, and the other allows a post-mortem Embrace, which Second Edition already accepts as possible without any special Discipline.<br /> <br /> So, look at the material you want to use in a Second Edition game, and pay attention to what it does. Gives Attribute bonuses, lets you ride the wave, gives you a weapon, banishes a ghost? The Attributes are all still the same and used the same, riding the wave still exists, weapons exist (but use the weapon rating rule of thumb above for 2e weapon rules), ghosts exist and have the same traits and can be banished. Alters the use of Virtue or Vice, causes or cures derangements, protects from the Predator's Taint? Those will send you to the rewriting desk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T07:44:47-07:00","id":1447816,"title":"","content":"I wish OOP would be more willing to give old content a 2.0 facelift, because to me it feels like a lot of the world now is just blanks that aren't filled in <i>unless </i>you played 1.0 and have those books (which I did for a little bit, but alas, I don't have any of the old books).<br /> <br /> Also it feels like OPP gave up on the Chronicles of Darkness, or put it on the back burner or something. As a point of comparison, in the nine years between Vampire: the Requiem 1.0 being released and the Strix Chronicles 2.0 book, there was an immense amount of supplements and additional content: individual covenant books, ghouls book, VII book, several bloodlines books, Belial's brood, individual clan books, etc, etc. Vampire 2.0 has now been out for eight years (one less the total lifespan of 2.0), and we have what, three vampire supplements in total, with bits and pieces scattered in the Dark Ages books?<br /> <br /> There's a hoard of vampire lore, information, and flavour already written, but for someone who got into the nWoD/CoD primarily after the 2.0 update, it just feels like I am missing <b>a lot</b> of knowledge/history/tradition/flavour that long-term players have. Basically new people coming to the gameline are just missing out on a lot of good stuff. A point of comparison: would a 2.0 player really understand what being Sworn in Ordo Dracul really means (and from what I remember that it is kind of a significat deal) just from the information published in the 2.0 books?<br /> <br /> I just want to get more immersed in this super detailed world but I am not going to pay money for 1.0 books.<br /> <br /> It's the same for werewolf, mage, changeling, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","user":"Vintervalpen","date":". 05-07-2021, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T09:27:04-07:00","id":1447822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1447745-how-hard-would-it-be-to-convert-1e-content-to-2e?p=1447816#post1447816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also it feels like OPP gave up on the Chronicles of Darkness, or put it on the back burner or something. As a point of comparison, in the nine years between Vampire: the Requiem 1.0 being released and the Strix Chronicles 2.0 book, there was an immense amount of supplements and additional content: individual covenant books, ghouls book, VII book, several bloodlines books, Belial's brood, individual clan books, etc, etc. Vampire 2.0 has now been out for eight years (one less the total lifespan of 2.0), and we have what, three vampire supplements in total, with bits and pieces scattered in the Dark Ages books?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the nine years between Requiem 1.0 and Strix Chronicles, there was an RPG boom, White Wolf changed ownership twice, Onyx Path was made and licensed the IPs from the new ownership, one of those owners wouldn't let them make the rules updates explicitly a new edition of the games, and the initial state of the new publishing company had been described to me as &quot;the creative director coordinating freelancers from his kitchen,&quot; in contrast to the days where physical print media was the main output of the company.<br /> <br /> In the eight years since Requiem 2.0 came out, it <i>re-</i> came out as a formal second edition, the new-new ownership made them change the name of the umbrella franchise so the could push what used to be &quot;classic World of Darkness,&quot; a global pandemic has been going on for over a year, a bunch of stuff has happened to cut into the group of established freelancers from the first edition books, and we've had a bunch of anthology books of the sort that have previously served as test runs for a new batch of freelancers to provide content to build a case on, in addition to the introduction of the STV as a venue for fanwork.<br /> <br /> 2004-2013 was a different time to 2013-2021.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T13:33:49-07:00","id":1447838,"title":"","content":"On top of that, there's a fine line to walk regarding updating old books; esp. if the majority of the content in them hasn't changed much. Fans don't always react well to retreads even if the quality of the new book is fine.<br /> <br /> That's how we get things like Secrets of the Covenants instead of five full Covenant supplements. Half-Damned also covers things that here spread between multiple supplements back in 1e.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that a lot of the end stage 1e supplements were being written during the development of Blood &amp; Smoke/2e, and were written to be largely cross-compatible (the Clan books sans mechanics [most of which are in VtR 2e core anyway], the blood sorcery book, etc.). So redoing those isn't going to be a high priority.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T13:57:34-07:00","id":1447841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1447745-how-hard-would-it-be-to-convert-1e-content-to-2e?p=1447822#post1447822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the nine years between Requiem 1.0 and Strix Chronicles, there was an RPG boom, White Wolf changed ownership twice, Onyx Path was made and licensed the IPs from the new ownership, one of those owners wouldn't let them make the rules updates explicitly a new edition of the games, and the initial state of the new publishing company had been described to me as &amp;quot;the creative director coordinating freelancers from his kitchen,&amp;quot; in contrast to the days where physical print media was the main output of the company.<br /> <br /> In the eight years since Requiem 2.0 came out, it <i>re-</i> came out as a formal second edition, the new-new ownership made them change the name of the umbrella franchise so the could push what used to be &amp;quot;classic World of Darkness,&amp;quot; a global pandemic has been going on for over a year, a bunch of stuff has happened to cut into the group of established freelancers from the first edition books, and we've had a bunch of anthology books of the sort that have previously served as test runs for a new batch of freelancers to provide content to build a case on, in addition to the introduction of the STV as a venue for fanwork.<br /> <br /> 2004-2013 was a different time to 2013-2021.</div> </div> </div> </div>And on top of that, it is not OPP\u2019s call what books going into production. It is Paradox\u2019s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T16:54:53-07:00","id":1447867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1447745-how-hard-would-it-be-to-convert-1e-content-to-2e?p=1447838#post1447838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the blood sorcery book</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Interesting.<br /> <br /> I might start buying into those things now that my Mage collection is complete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T17:10:44-07:00","id":1447869,"title":"","content":"Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies's rules were used to revamp the costs of rituals in 2e and AFAIK remains the official guideline for ritual creation for Theban Sorcery and Cruac. Even if you don't use the system in it for a more flexible form of blood sorcery, it still works for designing rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T21:13:41-07:00","id":1447890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1447745-how-hard-would-it-be-to-convert-1e-content-to-2e?p=1447869#post1447869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies's rules were used to revamp the costs of rituals in 2e and AFAIK remains the official guideline for ritual creation for Theban Sorcery and Cruac. Even if you don't use the system in it for a more flexible form of blood sorcery, it still works for designing rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which, fun fact, is in fact exactly what I did when I wrote the Kimiya Sorceries for 1001 Nightmares. S&amp;B is a great book!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"