hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T10:43:29-07:00","id":1447951,"title":"","content":"As Far As I Know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T20:59:56-07:00","id":1448017,"title":"","content":"Yeah, to echo the above, there are a lot of valid reasons why 2e content has been sparse and slow-moving compared to 1e.<br /> <br /> I will say on the subject of retreads that there's some stuff that probably could (and should) be reorganized and reprinted, especially for books that have been out of print and hard to find (as a physical book and not a PDF, anyway) for a very, very long time, like Immortals. I'm not sure if I ever even laid eyes on a physical copy of that title before I discovered it was out of print.<br /> <br /> Other 1e books could probably have the info compiled or compressed in a rework for 2e; Requiem, as an example, had I believe three separate books for Bloodlines before they made the jump to Strix, not to mention the ones out of the core book and spread throughout other supplements. I'd be fine with paying for one big compendium of 1e Bloodlines that received the required changes to both lore and mechanics to fit in and function easily in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26615-runomai","name":"RuNoMai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T10:15:57-07:00","id":1448053,"title":"","content":"On the subject of Bloodlines I feel like it would be remiss of me not to mention <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/301087/Bloodlines-The-Devoted\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: the Devoted</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/281799/Bloodlines-The-Resurrected\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: the Resurrected</a> on Storyteller's Vault. Collectively these books update about 50 first edition Bloodlines to second edition. Since it's community content YMMV but these books are both of very high quality and I haven't found anything too broken or problematic in them. I've given my players a green light to use any of the Bloodlines in these books in our Requiem 2e game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T10:46:23-07:00","id":1448054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1447745-how-hard-would-it-be-to-convert-1e-content-to-2e?p=1448053#post1448053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of Bloodlines I feel like it would be remiss of me not to mention <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/301087/Bloodlines-The-Devoted\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: the Devoted</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/281799/Bloodlines-The-Resurrected\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: the Resurrected</a> on Storyteller's Vault. Collectively these books update about 50 first edition Bloodlines to second edition. Since it's community content YMMV but these books are both of very high quality and I haven't found anything too broken or problematic in them. I've given my players a green light to use any of the Bloodlines in these books in our Requiem 2e game</div> </div> </div> </div>Also worth noting that while it is community content, there are a couple of freelancers on those projects (yours truly included) and they are overseen by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a>, who has done plenty on Requiem 2e. So they aren't official, but they are about as darn close as you are getting. Which is actually another good reason for new books to have new content and not rehash the old stuff. The Vault is a great place to do those conversions. <br /> <br /> We'd also be remiss not to mention <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/323224/Strange-Shades-Mekhet?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Shades</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/342865/Better-Feared-Nosferatu?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Better Feared</a>, which fill the same niche for updating the Clanbooks. False Gods, the Ventrue book, is coming soon and there are plans for more community content updates in motion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T11:58:52-07:00","id":1448057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1447745-how-hard-would-it-be-to-convert-1e-content-to-2e?p=1448054#post1448054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also worth noting that while it is community content, there are a couple of freelancers on those projects (yours truly included) and they are overseen by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a>, who has done plenty on Requiem 2e. So they aren't official, but they are about as darn close as you are getting. Which is actually another good reason for new books to have new content and not rehash the old stuff. The Vault is a great place to do those conversions.<br /> <br /> We'd also be remiss not to mention <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/323224/Strange-Shades-Mekhet?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Shades</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/342865/Better-Feared-Nosferatu?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Better Feared</a>, which fill the same niche for updating the Clanbooks. False Gods, the Ventrue book, is coming soon and there are plans for more community content updates in motion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also endorse these products and sentiments.<br /> <br /> As for conversion stuff, well, I've obviously thought a lot about this. A few things are really straightforward, especially as you get toward the end of the first edition, though as someone said above, it depends on how radically different the 2E version of the game is from 1E. With things like <b>Promethean</b>, there's some mechanical drift, but you can eyeball it; with things like <b>Geist</b>, you have to start from scratch.<br /> <br /> You also come across things that are just...bad. I have a great fondness for 1E CofD (I quite literally own every book in hardcover), but it suffered from some really bad design choices early on. That's not to be snitty, but the first days of &quot;NWoD&quot; had some systems that needed <i>work</i>. Having gone through pretty much every bloodline in <b>Vampire </b>now, my expert opinion is that the vast majority of them, mechanically speaking, have nothing worth preserving. And let's not even start on how some of the weaknesses are paragraphs and paragraphs and PARAGRAPHS long for no discernible reason.<br /> <br /> Some of this is a product of 2E being a bit more rigorous with its power-level, but there are genuinely 1E Disciplines at the fourth level that just let you know someone's Virtue and Vice, or give you +2 to...stuff (and that's after paying 50 experience in 2004 dollars). Which is a long way of saying, some things can't be converted without completely remaking them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 05-09-2021, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T14:28:23-07:00","id":1448804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1447745-how-hard-would-it-be-to-convert-1e-content-to-2e?p=1448057#post1448057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> or give you +2 to...stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>2e Disciplines, of course, scale the Stuff bonus to the Discipline rating.<br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah, generally speaking, there's a difference between &quot;make it work in 2e&quot; and &quot;give it a proper 2e treatment.&quot; The former is very easy, as you can just shift needed mechanics slightly and call it good; derangement becomes persistent condition, penalty to using hand becomes Arm Wrack, etc. The latter is more difficult and requires you to get to the foundation of what the content is about, in more complex cases like bloodlines, and make it fit 2e design philosophies. Which, let's be honest, is something even some later 2e supplements don't properly do. (I'm looking at you, Spilled Blood, with your two bloodlines lacking any bonuses and your bloodline discipline that's as brokenly inconsistent as any 1e one)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T16:22:42-07:00","id":1448815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1447745-how-hard-would-it-be-to-convert-1e-content-to-2e?p=1448804#post1448804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e Disciplines, of course, scale the Stuff bonus to the Discipline rating.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Stuff bonuses are the heart of the game. I think a lot about Stuff bonuses.<br /> <br /> ...that's both a joke and a slightly disturbing realization that I <i>do </i>think a lot about random dice modifiers.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}